# Fastmail's Masked Email (src/sync/masked_email.rs) and DuckDuckGo Email
# Protection (src/sync/forwarding.rs), in Forwarding settings.

masked-email-make-an-api-token-in-fastmail = Make an API token in Fastmail's settings (Privacy & Security → API tokens) with access to Masked Email.

masked-email-copy-the-token-duckduckgo = Copy the token from DuckDuckGo Email Protection's autofill settings.

masked-email-or-use-an-account-added-here = Or use the Fastmail account you added here, without a token:

masked-email-enter-an-api-token = Enter an API token.

masked-email-the-token-has-a-space = The token has a space or line break in it; copy it again.

masked-email-couldnt-reach-fastmail = Couldn't reach Fastmail

masked-email-fastmail-didnt-accept-the-token = Fastmail didn't accept the token. Check that it has access to Masked Email.

masked-email-fastmail-answered = Fastmail answered { $status }

masked-email-fastmail-sent-a-reply-picacho-cant-read = Fastmail sent a reply Picacho can't read

masked-email-fastmail-refused = Fastmail refused it ({ $kind }){ $detail }

masked-email-this-token-cant-use-masked-email = This token can't use Masked Email. Make one with access to Masked Email.

masked-email-this-account-has-no-masked-email = This account has no Masked Email: only Fastmail accounts do, and only when their sign-in may use it.

masked-email-the-fastmail-account-is-gone = The Fastmail account these masked addresses belong to is no longer in Picacho.

masked-email-fastmail-cant-do-this = Masked Email can't do this.

masked-email-turn-duck-addresses-off-on-duckduckgo = Duck Addresses can only be turned off on DuckDuckGo's own site.

masked-email-forget-it-keeps-forwarding = Forget { $email }? DuckDuckGo keeps forwarding its mail until you deactivate it on DuckDuckGo's site.

masked-email-forget = Forget

masked-email-forget-address = Forget Address…
